# 👥 HR Workforce Analytics Dashboard

An interactive multi-page Power BI dashboard designed to analyze workforce distribution, employee attrition, job satisfaction, salary trends, and workforce risk factors using HR analytics data. 

---

# 📊 Project Overview

This project focuses on transforming HR data into actionable workforce insights that support employee retention, operational planning, and workforce optimization.

The dashboard helps organizations:

* Monitor employee attrition trends
* Identify high-risk workforce segments
* Analyze salary and overtime impact
* Evaluate department and job role performance
* Improve retention strategies using data-driven insights

---

# 🚀 Dashboard Pages

## 📌 Page 1 — Workforce Overview

Provides a high-level summary of workforce composition and attrition performance.

### Dashboard Includes

* Total Employees
* Attrition Count
* Attrition Rate
* Average Salary
* Average Age
* Gender Distribution
* Attrition by Department
* Attrition by Age Group
* Job Role Distribution

### Key Insights

* Overall attrition rate stands at approximately **16%**
* Employees aged **26–35** experienced the highest attrition
* Research & Development showed the highest employee exits
* Sales Executive and Laboratory Technician roles recorded elevated turnover
* Workforce gender distribution remained relatively balanced

---

## 📌 Page 2 — Employee Satisfaction & Retention Analysis

Focused on understanding retention drivers and employee engagement.

### Analysis Includes

* Attrition by Salary Range
* Attrition by Overtime
* Attrition by Work-Life Balance
* Attrition by Job Satisfaction
* Attrition by Years at Company

### Key Insights

* Employees earning below **$5K/month** showed the highest attrition risk
* Overtime strongly correlated with employee turnover
* Lower job satisfaction levels increased attrition probability
* Employees with fewer years at the company experienced higher turnover
* Poor work-life balance contributed significantly to employee exits

---

## 📌 Page 3 — High-Risk Workforce Analysis

Focused on identifying departments and roles with elevated attrition exposure.

### Analysis Includes

* Attrition Risk by Salary & Overtime
* High-Risk Employee Profiles
* Attrition by Job Role
* Attrition by Department & Job Satisfaction

### Key Insights

* Laboratory Technicians and Sales Executives were among the highest-risk roles
* High overtime combined with low salary increased attrition significantly
* Research & Development and Sales departments experienced the highest workforce instability
* Employees with low satisfaction levels were more likely to leave

